WEBVTT

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.200
Let's see... Where do I even start?

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.700
My name is Funada Kathleen.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:41.170
I'm eighteen, and I didn't 
graduate from high school.

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:45.550
I want to leave a record of what 
I'm about to say right now.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.780
And to prove that I was actually here.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:51.970
Not that it matters anymore.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.580
It's currently 2030.

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.360
This is Tokyo.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.720
Sumida Ward, to be precise,

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.900
though it doesn't exist anymore.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.300
It's all gone.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.210
I think it was about two years ago 
that those things showed up.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.790
It came out of nowhere.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.960
I think I first saw them on the news.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.050
At first, they said it was an epidemic,

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.930
and that they successfully contained it.

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:23.810
Supposedly they built some kind 
of facility overseas to do that.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:28.310
Everyone said it was probably 
something like mad cow disease.

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:31.450
They said something about 
irregularities and prions in the brain,

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.810
and cases of violence related to that.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.380
Some people claimed it was 
a military conspiracy

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.820
or some movie promotion, too.

00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:43.620
<i>This disease that started 
in Venice has been named Gibiate</i>

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.570
<i>and is spreading all across the world.</i>

00:01:46.110 --> 00:01:49.210
<i>Countries across the world 
are researching countermeasures</i>

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:51.840
<i>and strongly encouraging their 
citizens to exercise caution.</i>

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.590
Apparently, the first case 
of this mysterious disease

00:01:56.590 --> 00:02:01.230
occurred in a woman visiting 
Venice on August 21st, 2028.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.460
At first, even the military was deployed  
and they successfully contained it,

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:10.930
but after that, infections spread 
at an explosive rate.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:14.950
We had no choice but 
to accept what was going on.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:19.730
This is footage from one of our choppers.

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:21.230
We're right above Tokyo.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:23.420
This is unbelievable.

00:02:23.420 --> 00:02:26.520
There are monsters appearing everywhere.

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.850
Do not gather in large groups.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.300
Please travel with 
as few people as possible!

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:34.040
What is that?

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.100
Oh, no! It can't be!

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:57.080
That's when everything changed.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.700
But I'm not going to give up.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:07.160
I'm going to create a vaccine 
and turn this world back to normal!

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.290
Please, God...

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:17.680
Grant me strength.

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:30.620
<b>1600 AD (Keicho Year 5)
October 15th</b>

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:53.880
Say, aren't you Kanzaki Sensui?

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:59.550
Indeed. And you are Sanada Kenroku,

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:00.680
I believe.

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:03.940
Wow, I'm surprised you remember.

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:06.470
You were actually 
on the winning side at Sekigahara,

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:08.510
so how'd you get exiled?

00:04:11.110 --> 00:04:12.500
A lot has happened.

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.650
Sensui!

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:20.620
I beg of you!

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.420
I have so much left to do in my life!

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.820
Please tell them that my army sided 
with Toyotomi at Sekigahara

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:32.320
solely on your orders as samurai general!

00:04:33.470 --> 00:04:35.240
If that is your wish, my lord.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:39.190
If we manage to settle this within the clan,

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:42.550
then Tokugawa-dono won't 
demand too much from us!

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:45.140
I'll have you sentenced 
to exile rather than death,

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:49.040
so once matters have settled down, 
I promise I'll summon you back here!

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:51.620
As you wish.

00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:00.080
Why did you get exiled?

00:05:02.020 --> 00:05:05.200
I did manage to settle down 
with a nice little lady,

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.590
but then I happened to give an evil 
magistrate his one-way ticket to Hell.

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:13.880
They caught me, but I'll take 
exile over execution any day.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:29.690
Wh-What the hell?!

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:40.470
Oh, come on! Don't tell me 
we're going out like this!

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:43.840
<i>My lord!</i>

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.880
<b>"Spirited Away"</b>

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:41.600
Where...

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:50.420
A castle?

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:57.830
Looks like we were carried somewhere else.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:00.790
Is this the afterlife?

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:08.130
I can't see the ocean.

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:10.460
But...

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:13.810
Did mankind build this?

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:19.800
Where are we?

00:08:18.930 --> 00:08:22.940
<b>Sumida Ward</b>

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:43.710
There's someone!

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:46.870
Hey, are you all right?!

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:49.600
Where are we?

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:21.200
Sensui!

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:31.850
What?!

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:36.130
What is going on here...?

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:37.850
Is it some apparition?

00:09:56.710 --> 00:09:59.440
<i>Will this even work on it?</i>

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.120
This is bad!

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:44.410
<i>Guess I didn't think that far ahead.</i>

00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:59.240
<i>This thing's not as fast as I expected.</i>

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.270
<i>Can I beat it?</i>

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:03.150
Kenroku!

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:38.470
This way, hurry!

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:41.720
It won't last long!

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:44.830
Get over here! Jump in, quick!

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:47.220
Kathleen-chan?!

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:50.340
Maeda-san, hold on a minute!

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:54.860
I'll make it quick!

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:07.920
There.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:09.290
Follow me.

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:20.010
Kathleen-chan!

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:26.050
What's with this wagon?!

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:28.240
It's faster than a horse!

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:38.240
These portable rations don't taste good,
but you're welcome to have some if you'd like.

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:42.410
Thanks! My stomach wouldn't 
stop growling, so this is perfect!

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:45.440
That's good!

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:46.790
Here.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:50.540
You have my gratitude.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:53.860
By the way, is this the afterlife?

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:54.700
Huh?

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:58.040
Th-This is Tokyo.

00:12:58.990 --> 00:13:01.670
Where did you two come from?

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:05.080
Those outfits you're wearing 
are a rare sight nowadays.

00:13:08.610 --> 00:13:10.270
Where?

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:14.370
If I remember right, we were a few 
dozen ri out from Edo on a boat.

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:16.240
Yes.

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:18.350
Edo?!

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:22.260
Those outfits, and the way you talk...

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:24.990
Don't tell me, y-you're samurai?!

00:13:25.380 --> 00:13:27.490
Huh?! Samurai?!

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:29.440
Wow!

00:13:29.440 --> 00:13:31.730
This is Edo, in the future.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:37.250
What do you mean, "the future"?

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.830
You're saying this is Edo?

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:43.900
Several centuries have passed 
since the Edo period you knew.

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:47.590
The world has become a place that's much
easier for the common people to live in.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:52.230
Japan hasn't seen any war 
for over 80 years now.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:57.600
But two years ago 
a disease began to spread...

00:13:57.600 --> 00:13:59.070
And that disease...

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:03.610
has turned everyone into monsters 
like the one you just saw.

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:05.610
Everyone?!

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:10.410
What did we shed all that blood for, then?!

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:14.680
I find that story hard to believe,

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:20.130
but I guess that means we fought 
for the world to turn out like this.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:23.400
Please don't think your 
battles were meaningless.

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:27.260
After all, we're still alive!

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:31.830
And we'll fight for our survival 
once again tomorrow!

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:38.530
Well, assuming this is Edo for now,

00:14:38.530 --> 00:14:42.860
you're saying the thing we just fought 
was one of the people with that disease?

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:49.630
That was a Gibia.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:52.870
It was human, once.

00:14:53.890 --> 00:14:58.120
It changed right before my eyes, 
so I thought it might be, but...

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:00.940
Hey, if that's caused by some disease,

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:03.880
does that mean we're infected already?

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:06.040
Don't worry about that!

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:09.630
Unless you're stung by the Gibia's stinger, 
you won't get infected.

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:10.890
Really?!

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:13.310
Phew, I panicked for a moment there.

00:15:15.730 --> 00:15:18.240
<i>This was a world of peace, then.</i>

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:21.950
<i>Before the Gibia showed up.</i>

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:35.620
I'm still surprised, though.

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:39.570
I never imagined I'd run into 
a real samurai while I still lived.

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:42.700
This is like some period drama.

00:15:42.700 --> 00:15:46.340
By the way, Samurai-san, 
what happened to your sword?

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:53.600
It would seem I arrived in this land 
with only what was on me.

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:57.110
I don't need mine since I'm a shinobi,

00:15:57.110 --> 00:16:01.320
but you're not much without 
your sword, are you, Sensui?

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:05.040
Are you strong, Samurai-san?

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:10.740
He's well known as Sensui, 
Slayer of a Thousand.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:13.170
Y-You're that strong?!

00:16:13.170 --> 00:16:15.530
I-I have a sword at my house!

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:17.500
It's nearby, so I'll go grab it!

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:20.430
Kathleen-chan, take over driving for a bit!

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:21.480
Huh?

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:23.810
It's dangerous to get out here!

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:24.860
Maeda-san!

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:26.310
Maeda-san?!

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:27.990
Don't worry, I'll be fine!

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:30.010
Just head on to the camp without me!

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:40.200
<i>It would be nice if he is that strong.</i>

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.720
This is our camp.

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:04.900
There's less than a hundred of us, 
but everyone's a good person.

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:12.530
Kath, you're back!

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:13.670
Did it go okay?

00:17:13.670 --> 00:17:14.760
Brian!

00:17:15.640 --> 00:17:17.760
Hmm? Who are they?

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:19.440
Uhh...

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:22.270
Okay, introduce yourselves.

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:24.930
I am Kanzaki Sensui.

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:26.770
Sanada Kenroku.

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:30.480
I'm Brian. I'm a marine.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.840
We welcome you to our camp.

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:36.190
We don't have any tatami mats, 
but make yourself at home.

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:43.200
What's with their outfits?

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.880
Hey, something new.

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:47.210
You think they're crazy?

00:17:45.730 --> 00:17:47.210
What odd outfits.

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:49.710
<i>We can hear you.</i>

00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:52.170
Everyone's a good person, huh.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:54.700
Hard for me to believe.

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:57.730
Newcomers are easily disliked.

00:17:58.400 --> 00:18:00.470
Welcome back, Kathleen.

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:01.950
Who are these men?

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:03.530
I'm home, Mom.

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:07.680
I brought a samurai and a ninja with me.

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:08.830
Real ones?

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:10.300
My, that's incredible!

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:14.280
I bet Maeda-san was overjoyed.

00:18:14.930 --> 00:18:17.740
So overjoyed he went to retrieve his sword.

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:20.620
Well, I'm off to visit the Doctor.

00:18:21.590 --> 00:18:24.480
You'll have to tell me all 
about the Edo period sometime.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:35.470
Your mother wasn't surprised 
when she heard about us.

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:38.620
Yeah.

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:46.790
My mother's so mentally broken she 
can't tell humans and Gibia apart.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:50.520
Doctor.

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:55.970
Who are those two?

00:18:56.620 --> 00:18:57.810
Well...

00:19:05.030 --> 00:19:07.500
A samurai traveled through time?!

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:10.510
Like I'd believe such nonsense!

00:19:10.510 --> 00:19:14.850
There are plenty of people who have 
lost their minds due to these times!

00:19:16.290 --> 00:19:19.670
I'm heading to Yokosuka 
to collect supplies tomorrow,

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:23.110
so you make sure these two 
don't steal anything!

00:19:23.110 --> 00:19:24.390
Got it?!

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:28.860
I managed to catch 
that he thinks we're crazy.

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:32.190
That man did use some strange words.

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:36.640
Adam might say mean things, 
but he's not a bad guy at heart.

00:19:37.750 --> 00:19:41.630
<i>We've already been transported to a place 
that might as well be the afterlife,</i>

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:44.990
<i>and now people are hating us 
for no reason, too.</i>

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:47.790
<i>Could our luck get any worse?!</i>

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:51.910
My name is Yoshinaga.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.260
I'm studying Gibiate,

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:58.550
the disease that transforms people 
into animal-like things.

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:01.140
I believe you two.

00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:03.140
After all, the Gibia exist.

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:07.310
It wouldn't be any stranger 
for samurai or ninja to be here.

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:10.690
What kind of creatures are those monsters?

00:20:10.690 --> 00:20:13.680
We call those creatures Gibia.

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:15.470
They used to be human.

00:20:16.300 --> 00:20:18.630
Once you're infected by the Gibia's venom

00:20:18.630 --> 00:20:21.770
the cells in your body begin
 to replicate abnormally,

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:24.180
altering the human chromosomes

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:26.950
and causing metamorphosis 
into a monstrous form.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:29.720
We're gradually coming to understand it,

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:32.090
but we believe that it's 
causing all of the information

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:35.950
gathered in a person's 
DNA throughout evolution

00:20:35.950 --> 00:20:38.680
to overreact and spin out of control.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:39.840
Have a look at this.

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:44.960
These are variations I've
seen throughout the world,

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:48.810
but those infected by the Gibia's venom

00:20:48.810 --> 00:20:53.550
transform into different varieties 
of Gibia based on age, race, and sex.

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:56.730
There's some individual variation,

00:20:56.730 --> 00:20:59.910
but once a victim is stung 
with a Gibia's stinger

00:20:59.910 --> 00:21:02.900
they transform into a monster 
within roughly five hours.

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:05.110
So, if you get stung, that's it?

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:06.870
Huh?! Were you stung?!

00:21:07.270 --> 00:21:08.350
Sensui?!

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:13.470
No, I only got hit by its fist, 
so I think I'm okay.

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:17.630
Sensui-kun, do you hear 
the sound of dripping water?

00:21:18.830 --> 00:21:19.880
No?

00:21:19.880 --> 00:21:21.970
Then you're fine.

00:21:21.970 --> 00:21:24.820
That's something else we've 
learned from our research.

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:27.130
Those who are infected by the Gibia Virus

00:21:27.130 --> 00:21:32.140
constantly hear the sound of water 
before they express symptoms.

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:33.640
The sound of water?

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:36.650
That's right. Deep within your ears.

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:39.900
Do you hear it, Sensui?!

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:46.090
No, I'm fine.

00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:48.410
I don't hear any water.

00:21:50.340 --> 00:21:51.630
Thank goodness.

00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:55.920
Also, getting stung doesn't 
necessarily mean you've been infected.

00:21:56.530 --> 00:21:58.690
Once a Gibia has used their stinger,

00:21:58.690 --> 00:22:03.210
the venom won't build up again 
for roughly 24 hours.

00:22:03.710 --> 00:22:05.930
You should remember that for future's sake.

00:22:10.450 --> 00:22:13.100
Hey, so what you were just saying...

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:14.960
You mean sometimes you'll still be okay

00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:17.440
even if the Gibia stings you 
with its stinger?

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:19.820
It's not that simple, though.

00:22:19.820 --> 00:22:24.250
They're driven by a strong 
impulse to spread,

00:22:24.250 --> 00:22:26.930
so even if they sting you 
and fail to inject any venom,

00:22:26.930 --> 00:22:29.450
they'll just grow stubborn 
and keep stinging you.

00:22:30.040 --> 00:22:32.020
Until you die.

00:22:32.820 --> 00:22:34.150
What the hell?

00:22:34.150 --> 00:22:38.680
Then, the only options are to die 
or become a Gibia and live?

00:22:39.350 --> 00:22:44.070
That's why we're researching 
a cure right now,

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:47.720
a drug to turn Gibia back into humans.

00:22:48.560 --> 00:22:50.440
<i>A desire to spread...</i>

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:54.230
<i>An urge to turn people into monsters...</i>

00:23:01.220 --> 00:23:02.840
It's so bright.

00:23:02.840 --> 00:23:04.730
There're so many torches.

00:23:05.110 --> 00:23:07.870
The Gibia dislike the light.

00:23:07.870 --> 00:23:11.370
So, when night falls, 
we turn on the camp's lights.

00:23:12.810 --> 00:23:15.240
Doctor, here.

00:23:18.140 --> 00:23:19.200
Good.

00:24:38.120 --> 00:25:10.020
<b>"Beyond the Maelstrom"</b>
